{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","generatedAt":"2026-07-25T02:30:00+00:00","scope":"1989 AP Calculus AB FRQs source-compared and independently solved; admin-only correction overlay.","defaults":{"verificationStatus":"independently-verified-source-compared","answerConfidence":1.0,"quality":{"completeness":"complete-verified","productionStatus":"teacher-archive-only","productionReadiness":0.98,"tutoringReadiness":0.98,"needsReview":true,"reviewReasons":["Rights/permission review required before public publication."],"transcriptionVerified":true,"answerVerified":true,"mediaVerified":true,"privateStudentAccess":true,"mathematicalVerificationPassed":true,"katexVerified":true,"mappingVerified":true,"studentReadyGatePassed":false},"studentEligible":false,"studentAccessible":false,"deploymentAccess":"teacher-archive-only","contentStatus":"complete","studentReady":false,"rubricStatus":"ECHS instructional solution generated after independent verification; official source scoring guideline unavailable.","audit":{"sourceChecked":true,"transcriptionStatus":"corrected","stemStatus":"verified","choicesStatus":"not_applicable","answerStatus":"verified","solutionStatus":"verified","katexStatus":"verified","mediaStatus":"verified","courseMappingStatus":"verified","unitMappingStatus":"verified","topicMappingStatus":"verified","lessonMappingStatus":"verified","calculatorStatus":"verified","overallStatus":"teacher-archive-only","correctionsMade":1,"reviewRequired":true,"reviewerNotes":"Rendered source page compared question-by-question and every part independently solved. The structured transcription, KaTeX, answers, media association, calculator designation, and mathematical mapping are verified. The record remains teacher/archive-only solely because public-publication permission is not established.","auditedAt":"2026-07-25T02:30:00+00:00"}},"records":[{"id":"APCALC-AB-FRQ-1989-01","prompt":"Let\n\\[\nf(x)=x^3-7x+6.\n\\]","parts":[{"label":"(a)","prompt":"Find the zeros.","answer":"\\[\nf(x)=(x-1)(x-2)(x+3),\n\\]\nso \\(\\boxed{x=-3,1,2}\\).","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]},{"label":"(b)","prompt":"Find the tangent line at \\(x=-1\\).","answer":"Since \\(f(-1)=12\\) and \\(f'(-1)=-4\\),\n\\[\n\\boxed{y=-4x+8}.\n\\]","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]},{"label":"(c)","prompt":"Find the number \\(c\\) from the Mean Value Theorem on \\([1,3]\\).","answer":"The average slope is \\(6\\). Solve \\(3c^2-7=6\\):\n\\[\n\\boxed{c=\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}}.\n\\]","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]}],"classification":{"primaryUnit":5,"primaryUnitLabel":"Unit 5: Analytical Applications of Differentiation","primaryTopic":"Mean Value Theorem","topicCode":"5.1","additionalTopics":["polynomial zeros","tangent line"],"lessonIds":["APCALC-U5"]},"audit":{"sourcePage":"33","correctionsMade":6}},{"id":"APCALC-AB-FRQ-1989-02","prompt":"Let \\(R\\) be the first-quadrant region enclosed by\n\\[\ny=\\sqrt{6x+4},\\qquad y=2x,\\qquad x=0.\n\\]","parts":[{"label":"(a)","prompt":"Find the area of \\(R\\).","answer":"The curves meet at \\(x=2\\). Thus\n\\[\nA=\\int_0^2(\\sqrt{6x+4}-2x)dx=\\boxed{\\frac{20}{9}}.\n\\]","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]},{"label":"(b)","prompt":"Set up, but do not evaluate, the volume when \\(R\\) is revolved about the \\(x\\)-axis.","answer":"\\[\n\\boxed{V=\\pi\\int_0^2\\left[(6x+4)-4x^2\\right]dx}.\n\\]","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]},{"label":"(c)","prompt":"Set up, but do not evaluate, the volume when \\(R\\) is revolved about the \\(y\\)-axis.","answer":"\\[\n\\boxed{V=2\\pi\\int_0^2x(\\sqrt{6x+4}-2x)dx}.\n\\]","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]}],"classification":{"primaryUnit":8,"primaryUnitLabel":"Unit 8: Applications of Integration","primaryTopic":"Area and Volume","topicCode":"8.8","additionalTopics":["radical function","washers","shells"],"lessonIds":["APCALC-U8"]},"audit":{"sourcePage":"33","correctionsMade":6}},{"id":"APCALC-AB-FRQ-1989-03","prompt":"A particle moves on the \\(x\\)-axis with\n\\[\na(t)=4\\cos(2t),\\qquad t\\ge0,\\qquad v(0)=1,\\qquad x(0)=0.\n\\]","parts":[{"label":"(a)","prompt":"Find the velocity.","answer":"\\[\n\\boxed{v(t)=1+2\\sin(2t)}.\n\\]","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]},{"label":"(b)","prompt":"Find the position.","answer":"\\[\n\\boxed{x(t)=t+1-\\cos(2t)}.\n\\]","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]},{"label":"(c)","prompt":"For \\(0<t<\\pi\\), when is the particle at rest?","answer":"Solve \\(1+2\\sin2t=0\\). The solutions are\n\\[\n\\boxed{t=\\frac{7\\pi}{12},\\frac{11\\pi}{12}}.\n\\]","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]}],"classification":{"primaryUnit":4,"primaryUnitLabel":"Unit 4: Contextual Applications of Differentiation","primaryTopic":"Rectilinear Motion","topicCode":"4.2","additionalTopics":["trigonometric acceleration","rest times"],"lessonIds":["APCALC-U4"]},"audit":{"sourcePage":"33","correctionsMade":6}},{"id":"APCALC-AB-FRQ-1989-04","prompt":"Let\n\\[\nf(x)=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x^2-4}}.\n\\]","parts":[{"label":"(a)","prompt":"Find the domain.","answer":"The denominator requires \\(x^2-4>0\\), so\n\\[\n\\boxed{(-\\infty,-2)\\cup(2,\\infty)}.\n\\]","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]},{"label":"(b)","prompt":"Find the vertical asymptotes.","answer":"\\[\n\\boxed{x=-2\\quad\\text{and}\\quad x=2}.\n\\]","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]},{"label":"(c)","prompt":"Find the horizontal asymptotes.","answer":"As \\(x\\to\\infty\\), \\(f(x)\\to1\\); as \\(x\\to-\\infty\\), \\(f(x)\\to-1\\). Thus \\(\\boxed{y=1,y=-1}\\).","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]},{"label":"(d)","prompt":"Find \\(f'(x)\\).","answer":"\\[\n\\boxed{f'(x)=-\\frac4{(x^2-4)^{3/2}}}.\n\\]","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]}],"classification":{"primaryUnit":3,"primaryUnitLabel":"Unit 3: Differentiation: Composite, Implicit, and Inverse Functions","primaryTopic":"Differentiation of Radical Quotients","topicCode":"3.3","additionalTopics":["domain","asymptotes"],"lessonIds":["APCALC-U3"]},"audit":{"sourcePage":"34","correctionsMade":7}},{"id":"APCALC-AB-FRQ-1989-05","prompt":"The source graph gives \\(f'\\) on \\([-10,10]\\). It crosses the \\(x\\)-axis at \\(x=-7,-1,4,8\\), has local maxima near \\(x=-3,6\\), and a local minimum at \\(x=2\\).","parts":[{"label":"(a)","prompt":"Where does \\(f\\) have horizontal tangents?","answer":"Where \\(f'(x)=0\\): \\(\\boxed{x=-7,-1,4,8}\\).","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]},{"label":"(b)","prompt":"Where does \\(f\\) have relative maxima?","answer":"The derivative changes positive to negative at \\(x=-1\\) and \\(x=8\\). Thus \\(\\boxed{x=-1,8}\\).","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]},{"label":"(c)","prompt":"Where is \\(f\\) concave downward?","answer":"The graph is concave downward where \\(f'\\) is decreasing: \\(\\boxed{(-3,2)\\cup(6,10)}\\).","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]}],"classification":{"primaryUnit":5,"primaryUnitLabel":"Unit 5: Analytical Applications of Differentiation","primaryTopic":"Interpreting a Derivative Graph","topicCode":"5.4","additionalTopics":["horizontal tangents","relative maxima","concavity"],"lessonIds":["APCALC-U5"]},"audit":{"sourcePage":"34","correctionsMade":6}},{"id":"APCALC-AB-FRQ-1989-06","prompt":"Oil remaining in a well satisfies\n\\[\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=ky,\\qquad y(0)=1{,}000{,}000,\\qquad y(6)=500{,}000.\n\\]\nPumping becomes unprofitable below \\(50{,}000\\) gallons.","parts":[{"label":"(a)","prompt":"Find \\(y(t)\\).","answer":"Since \\(e^{6k}=1/2\\), \\(k=-\\ln2/6\\). Thus\n\\[\n\\boxed{y(t)=1{,}000{,}000\\,2^{-t/6}}.\n\\]","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]},{"label":"(b)","prompt":"At what rate is oil decreasing when \\(y=600{,}000\\)?","answer":"\\[\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=ky=-100{,}000\\ln2.\n\\]\nSo it is decreasing at \\(\\boxed{100{,}000\\ln2\\text{ gallons/year}}\\).","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]},{"label":"(c)","prompt":"When should pumping stop?","answer":"Set \\(y=50{,}000\\):\n\\[\n2^{-t/6}=\\frac1{20},\\qquad \\boxed{t=\\frac{6\\ln20}{\\ln2}\\approx25.93\\text{ years}}.\n\\]","maxPoints":3,"rubric":[]}],"classification":{"primaryUnit":7,"primaryUnitLabel":"Unit 7: Differential Equations","primaryTopic":"Exponential Differential Equations","topicCode":"7.6","additionalTopics":["exponential decay","threshold time"],"lessonIds":["APCALC-U7"]},"audit":{"sourcePage":"34","correctionsMade":6}}]}